            <title>[LU-21336]  tests: h2name_or_ip() gives NIDs that LNet does not use</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21336</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;h2name_or_ip() in test-framework.sh builds a NID for each address from&lt;br/&gt;
"hostname -I" on the node.  The link-type filter added in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20173" title="sanity-sec test_31: unable to remount client (connection timed out)" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20173"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20173&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; only&lt;br/&gt;
removes addresses of the wrong link type.  On a node with more than one&lt;br/&gt;
ethernet interface it still returns several NIDs, but LNet listens on&lt;br/&gt;
only one of them.  A client given an extra NID as a failover peer of a&lt;br/&gt;
target retries it forever.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The workaround is to put the data IP in ${facet}_HOST instead of the&lt;br/&gt;
hostname, because h2name_or_ip() maps a literal IP to exactly one NID.&lt;br/&gt;
This makes the node lists harder to read and breaks name-based lookups&lt;br/&gt;
in test-framework.  For example, node_fstypes() compares its argument&lt;br/&gt;
with facet_host(), so yaml.sh reports file_system: "NA" for every&lt;br/&gt;
server.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;LNet already knows the right NIDs: host_nids_address() asks&lt;br/&gt;
"lctl list_nids".  h2name_or_ip() should use it and fall back to&lt;br/&gt;
"hostname -I" only when LNet is not loaded.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
